# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AIOS v0.1 ignore rules
#
# IMPORTANT — build products that are NOT ignored on purpose:
#   nn/config.h            <- generated by tools/train.py
#   nn/model_weights.h     <- generated by tools/train.py
#   tools/intent_corpus.json, tools/golden_features.json, tools/golden_vectors.json
#
# build.py:collect_sources() skips the whole nn/ and nlu/ directories when
# nn/config.h or nn/model_weights.h are absent, silently producing a kernel
# WITHOUT the NLU layer. test.py then fails. These files are generated, but they
# MUST stay tracked so that a fresh clone builds the full kernel.
#
# Same rule for the tools/*.json fixtures: they are the golden corpus/vectors
# referenced by test.py, so they must stay tracked too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Python -------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- Build outputs (regenerated by build.py) -----------------------------
# build/manifest.json and the *.log files inside build/ contain absolute
# paths of the machine that produced them, so the directory is ignored whole.
build/
aios.img
aios-hdd.img
*.elf
*.bin
*.o
*.exe
*.pdb

# ---- Virtual environments ------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Editors / IDEs / OS -------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Local scratch and developer session data -----------------------------
# .workbuddy/ holds machine-local agent session state: never publish it.
.workbuddy/
.scratch/

# ---- Ad-hoc one-off debug dumps kept at the repository root ---------------
/_*.txt
/_*.log
/_*.py
